WEBVTT

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:09.235 --> 01:10.904
The weather is so lovely!

01:10.987 --> 01:14.491
Yes, it's a good day to go hiking.

01:14.574 --> 01:16.618
Take off your sunglasses
before you fall on your face.

01:16.701 --> 01:17.535
Okay.

01:17.619 --> 01:19.120
- Hey, In-suk.
- Yeah?

01:19.204 --> 01:21.706
Your skin looks flawless today.

01:21.790 --> 01:22.791
- You think so?
- Yes.

01:23.541 --> 01:25.627
I guess my Botox injections
are finally working their magic.

01:25.710 --> 01:27.253
Wait, you had Botox? Where?

01:27.337 --> 01:29.547
- On my frown lines, my smile lines…
- And?

01:29.631 --> 01:31.299
and pretty much everywhere.

01:31.382 --> 01:33.468
- I don't approve of it.
- Why not?

01:33.551 --> 01:35.470
It just seems too artificial to me.

01:36.012 --> 01:39.015
What's most beautiful
is getting old naturally.

01:39.098 --> 01:41.226
Says the woman who uses
the most expensive cosmetics.

01:41.309 --> 01:43.061
I'm just respecting my skin.

01:43.144 --> 01:46.022
Sure, since our country
is all about respect.

01:47.982 --> 01:49.609
- Hey, Jae-suk.
- Yes?

01:49.692 --> 01:52.153
Did you do something to your face too?
You're glowing.

01:52.237 --> 01:55.698
I did a prune juice cleanse yesterday.

01:58.910 --> 02:00.120
I guess it was effective though.

02:00.203 --> 02:02.205
- It was.
- My goodness.

02:02.288 --> 02:03.832
I can't control my sphincter.

02:04.791 --> 02:06.292
What did you eat yesterday?

02:06.376 --> 02:07.877
- Prune juice.
- Prune juice!

02:07.961 --> 02:09.295
I can relate.

02:09.379 --> 02:10.839
I was looking at myself in the mirror

02:10.922 --> 02:12.924
and saw that my buttocks
looked like squashed tofu.

02:13.007 --> 02:14.717
They used to look like peaches, you know?

02:14.801 --> 02:15.718
- They were.
- I'm so upset.

02:15.802 --> 02:18.012
That's why we have to work out at our age.

02:18.096 --> 02:20.515
That's why we're going hiking, right?

02:20.598 --> 02:22.225
I'm not talking about hiking.

02:22.308 --> 02:24.269
- What then?
- Squeeze and release.

02:24.352 --> 02:26.312
- I can't do it well.
- What are you doing?

02:26.396 --> 02:27.564
Kegel exercises.

02:28.398 --> 02:30.108
- I'm off.
- Kegel exercises.

02:30.191 --> 02:32.527
- Squeeze and release.
- The air is so clean.

02:34.279 --> 02:35.530
Oh no!

02:35.613 --> 02:36.865
Hey!

02:36.948 --> 02:38.408
That smells!

02:38.491 --> 02:40.034
Hey, wait for me!

02:40.827 --> 02:42.537
Wait up!

02:43.163 --> 02:44.164
Hey!

02:45.081 --> 02:46.416
Don't come near me!

02:49.335 --> 02:50.879
My goodness. I can't believe you.

02:52.755 --> 02:56.467
Oh my, Mi-suk.
Did you buy a new hiking outfit?

02:56.551 --> 02:58.887
- Wow.
- The color is so pretty!

02:58.970 --> 03:01.723
Yes, I guess my taste changed with age.

03:01.806 --> 03:03.099
I love red clothes now.

03:03.182 --> 03:05.518
It's not a matter of taste but science.

03:05.602 --> 03:08.354
As we age,
changes in the retinal microvasculature

03:08.438 --> 03:11.399
make it harder for us to perceive
colors with short wavelengths like blue,

03:11.482 --> 03:15.153
as opposed to colors with long wavelengths
such as the color red.

03:15.236 --> 03:18.364
It must be nice to be so knowledgeable.

03:18.448 --> 03:21.075
This is made out of functional fabric.
You know "Core-Tex"?

03:21.159 --> 03:24.871
You mean "Gore-Tex," right?
Not "Core-Tex."

03:24.954 --> 03:28.082
That's right.
It was just a slip of the tongue.

03:28.166 --> 03:31.252
My daughter sent it to me from the US.
It's really expensive.

03:31.336 --> 03:33.421
- It looks expensive.
- It really does.

03:33.504 --> 03:35.048
Seok-ryu is a wonderful daughter.

03:35.131 --> 03:36.382
She's right.

03:37.967 --> 03:40.845
I don't feel comfortable
receiving gifts that my son bought

03:40.929 --> 03:41.971
with his hard-earned money.

03:42.055 --> 03:44.307
As if he ever gave you anything.

03:44.390 --> 03:48.436
I don't place much value
on such material things.

03:49.103 --> 03:53.316
The fact that my son, Seung-hyo, exists
is a gift in itself.

03:54.025 --> 03:55.985
Are you saying my daughter isn't?

03:56.069 --> 03:58.238
I didn't want to mention it
to avoid bragging,

03:58.321 --> 04:01.783
but Seung-hyo
recently met with the president.

04:01.866 --> 04:04.911
He designed a library that won an award
at an architecture competition,

04:04.994 --> 04:06.454
so the president personally came to visit

04:06.537 --> 04:09.624
and praised it as a superb model
of a public facility.

04:09.707 --> 04:11.209
Seung-hyo is so impressive.

04:11.292 --> 04:12.126
Of course.

04:12.710 --> 04:14.462
Listen, guys.

04:14.545 --> 04:17.173
Do you know who the second richest person
in the world is?

04:17.257 --> 04:19.217
- I do. It's Jaden Becker.
- Right.

04:19.300 --> 04:20.677
The CEO of Greip?

04:20.760 --> 04:23.930
Not everyone in the world will know
who the president of South Korea is,

04:24.013 --> 04:25.223
but everyone knows Jaden Becker.

04:25.306 --> 04:27.308
Every Friday night,

04:27.392 --> 04:29.560
he and Seok-ryu
shoot the breeze over some beer.

04:30.270 --> 04:33.606
It's all because she works in
the most prestigious company in the world

04:33.690 --> 04:35.733
after graduating from a top university
in the US.

04:37.026 --> 04:40.363
As you know, Seung-hyo was at the top
of his class at Hanguk University.

04:41.030 --> 04:43.199
Seok-ryu not only graduated early

04:43.283 --> 04:45.868
but also got offers
from all the top companies.

04:46.369 --> 04:48.246
Greip didn't pick Seok-ryu.

04:48.329 --> 04:50.456
She was the one who chose them.

04:51.040 --> 04:53.710
Seung-hyo helped design
the New York Art Center,

04:53.793 --> 04:55.878
which won an international
architecture award.

04:55.962 --> 04:58.214
He was the first Korean to do so!

04:58.923 --> 05:00.883
Seok-ryu is the best employee

05:00.967 --> 05:03.636
in that global company full of geniuses!

05:04.304 --> 05:07.181
You wouldn't believe
how much she earns just in incentives!

05:07.932 --> 05:12.937
You have to remember that Seung-hyo
was on the national swim team too.

05:13.021 --> 05:15.481
It's not easy for people
to excel in multiple areas,

05:15.565 --> 05:17.358
but my son does exactly that.

05:18.860 --> 05:21.612
Hey, Seok-ryu is a gift from heaven.

05:21.696 --> 05:24.032
You know what I dreamed about
when I became pregnant with her?

05:24.615 --> 05:26.951
- I was--
- You were in a rainbow-colored paradise

05:27.035 --> 05:28.578
- and found a huge tree there.
- Yes.

05:28.661 --> 05:31.414
You were entranced by it
and saw a juicy pomegranate.

05:31.497 --> 05:33.416
So you picked it
and got pregnant with Seok-ryu.

05:33.499 --> 05:35.501
- I memorized it all.
- Thanks.

05:35.585 --> 05:37.837
That sounds like some fairytale.
As for Seung-hyo--

05:37.920 --> 05:40.590
As for Seung-hyo,
you got assigned to work in France

05:40.673 --> 05:42.550
without knowing you were pregnant.

05:42.633 --> 05:45.595
And you dreamed about a blue dragon
rising out of the Seine.

05:45.678 --> 05:46.971
You remember all that?

05:47.055 --> 05:50.808
That's some extravagant founding myth
you have there.

05:50.892 --> 05:52.393
- Let me tell you…
- Unbelievable.

05:52.977 --> 05:55.980
Those two won't stop
talking about the same things.

05:56.064 --> 05:58.107
It's driving me crazy.

05:58.191 --> 06:01.319
They just want to brag
about their successful children.

06:02.737 --> 06:04.238
Who do you think will win today?

06:04.322 --> 06:06.032
- Hye-suk.
- Why her?

06:06.574 --> 06:08.826
Because she's a diplomat
and can be persuasive?

06:08.910 --> 06:11.496
No, because Seung-hyo
is receiving another award today.

06:33.267 --> 06:34.519
CHOI SEUNG-HYO

06:35.311 --> 06:36.312
Seung-hyo!

06:39.023 --> 06:40.233
Oh. It's you, sir.

06:40.316 --> 06:41.609
You're here.

06:41.692 --> 06:45.071
I thought only top celebrities
got to come to parties like this.

06:45.154 --> 06:46.989
Seung-hyo is such a star!

06:47.073 --> 06:47.949
Where is he?

06:48.032 --> 06:50.076
Seung-hyo? I don't know.

06:50.159 --> 06:51.077
What?

07:05.716 --> 07:07.552
CHOI SEUNG-HYO
CEO, REGISTERED ARCHITECT

07:08.761 --> 07:11.097
You want to design a memorial park?

07:11.681 --> 07:12.682
Yes.

07:12.765 --> 07:14.475
But why did you ask me to see me?

07:15.309 --> 07:17.562
I have visited
many funeral homes for research,

07:17.645 --> 07:20.148
but I don't think I've interviewed
any of the workers.

07:20.231 --> 07:24.026
I heard that you've worked
as a funeral director for 20 years.

07:24.110 --> 07:25.278
Has it been that long?

07:26.821 --> 07:28.448
In all my years doing this job,

07:28.531 --> 07:31.367
I've never had anyone
ask to interview me before.

07:31.951 --> 07:32.869
I see.

07:34.954 --> 07:36.539
I want to do a good job.

07:37.248 --> 07:38.207
A proper job

07:38.291 --> 07:39.542
with sincerity.

07:42.587 --> 07:45.506
I don't know how much help I'd be.

07:45.590 --> 07:47.758
Just tell me what you honestly felt

07:47.842 --> 07:50.428
while working on this job.

07:52.555 --> 07:56.434
To tell you the truth,
my mother passed away not long ago.

07:57.310 --> 08:00.021
I'm sorry for your loss.

08:00.605 --> 08:03.357
Everyone has to go through it
sooner or later.

08:04.609 --> 08:07.069
But it was a comfort to me

08:07.153 --> 08:10.031
that I could send her off beautifully
with my own two hands.

08:10.114 --> 08:12.533
I'm sure your mother was glad to know

08:12.617 --> 08:14.577
that her daughter
was there to see her off.

08:14.660 --> 08:15.578
I agree.

08:17.163 --> 08:18.456
That is why

08:19.332 --> 08:22.251
I want people to visit
with a sense of gladness as well.

08:30.259 --> 08:34.472
Memorial parks don't always have to be
so solemn and sad.

08:35.056 --> 08:36.974
The people resting here were once alive.

08:37.934 --> 08:40.228
They are all beloved friends
and family members.

08:47.485 --> 08:51.280
What if we build
a Shelter for Memories in the lobby?

08:52.949 --> 08:55.535
It would look like
a small library or a café.

08:56.827 --> 08:59.705
We'd fill it up with things
that the departed used to love,

08:59.789 --> 09:00.790
like books and music.

09:01.332 --> 09:04.460
So the people who are visiting
their loved ones can reminisce.

09:05.253 --> 09:06.379
Of course they'd be sad,

09:07.296 --> 09:10.132
but I want their tears to be
interspersed with warm smiles too.

09:10.633 --> 09:11.801
I love it.

09:13.594 --> 09:15.346
How did you come up with such an idea?

09:17.098 --> 09:17.932
I'm sorry.

09:19.016 --> 09:20.268
I have to take this.

09:23.854 --> 09:24.689
Hello.

09:25.773 --> 09:28.401
I can't really talk right now, Myeong-u.

09:28.484 --> 09:31.654
Where the heck are you?
The awards ceremony is starting soon!

09:32.863 --> 09:34.782
I'll be right there.

09:36.909 --> 09:39.036
Through a design that harmonizes
with the environment…

09:39.120 --> 09:41.497
It's almost Seung-hyo's turn
to go up on stage.

09:42.665 --> 09:44.166
Did he say he'll make it in time?

09:45.918 --> 09:47.044
What are you doing?

09:47.628 --> 09:51.048
I mean, I'm the co-CEO
of Architectural Firm Atelier In,

09:51.132 --> 09:53.134
so I should accept the award in his stead.

09:53.217 --> 09:56.596
Next, we will announce
the winner of the Creative Award.

09:56.679 --> 09:57.763
Oh no.

09:57.847 --> 10:00.933
The Creative Award
for the 2024 Magazine Awards

10:01.017 --> 10:02.727
- goes to…
- No.

10:03.394 --> 10:07.106
architect and co-CEO
of the architectural firm, Atelier In,

10:07.189 --> 10:08.441
Choi Seung-hyo.

10:08.983 --> 10:10.693
- I'll be back.
- Wait, no.

10:11.402 --> 10:12.445
- What?
- What?

10:12.528 --> 10:14.196
- Hey, Myeong-u.
- Seung-hyo!

10:14.280 --> 10:15.990
- I'm not late, right?
- Right.

10:16.741 --> 10:18.868
Look who's finally here.

10:18.951 --> 10:20.494
The star got here just in time.

10:20.578 --> 10:23.164
With a face like that,
he has to be a star.

10:26.125 --> 10:30.004
CREATIVE AWARD

10:30.588 --> 10:33.674
Let's hear Mr. Choi Seung-hyo's
acceptance speech.

10:38.387 --> 10:39.597
Thank you.

10:42.266 --> 10:45.311
I told him to prepare
an acceptance speech beforehand.

10:45.394 --> 10:46.979
He should've spoken longer

10:47.063 --> 10:49.065
for the cameras to capture his beauty
from all angles.

10:49.148 --> 10:52.318
Hey! Our name!
You forgot to mention our name!

10:54.654 --> 10:57.823
I'm from the architectural firm,
Atelier In.

10:57.907 --> 10:59.367
Please give him a round of applause.

11:08.250 --> 11:10.503
Yahoo!

11:10.586 --> 11:14.131
Yelling "yahoo" at the top of a mountain
is so old-fashioned.

11:14.215 --> 11:16.384
Who cares if it's old-fashioned?

11:16.467 --> 11:17.760
I'm respecting the mountain.

11:17.843 --> 11:19.512
You'll get reported to the police.

11:19.595 --> 11:22.098
Who's going to report me? You?

11:22.181 --> 11:25.059
Those two are still going at it.

11:25.142 --> 11:28.145
They're wasting energy
fighting and making up all the time.

11:28.229 --> 11:29.271
I know, right?

11:29.355 --> 11:30.356
Hey.

11:31.565 --> 11:33.025
I have something for you guys.

11:33.609 --> 11:34.527
- What?
- What is it?

11:35.111 --> 11:36.487
Seok-ryu's wedding invitation?

11:36.570 --> 11:38.948
Wow, look at this.

11:39.657 --> 11:41.659
I held off giving them to you

11:41.742 --> 11:43.994
because I wanted to present them
in a special place.

11:44.078 --> 11:46.705
Why did you print the invitations
when the wedding will be held in the US?

11:46.789 --> 11:48.374
I didn't want to miss out on anything.

11:48.874 --> 11:51.627
Look at this. It's so beautiful.

11:51.710 --> 11:55.756
You must be so happy
that your daughter's getting married.

11:55.840 --> 11:58.300
You now have a weight off your shoulders!

11:58.384 --> 11:59.468
That's right.

11:59.552 --> 12:04.890
When will I get my loser daughter
out of my house?

12:04.974 --> 12:07.393
- Mo-eum will find someone soon.
- She will.

12:07.476 --> 12:10.813
Oh right. Is Seung-hyo
going out with anyone these days?

12:10.896 --> 12:13.065
- No, he's way too busy.
- I see.

12:13.149 --> 12:16.402
That's just an excuse.
Even busy people can find time to date.

12:16.485 --> 12:19.530
Seok-ryu managed to find someone
even though she was so busy.

12:19.613 --> 12:22.575
I told you that my son-in-law
is an international lawyer, right?

12:22.658 --> 12:23.659
- Hey.
- It's so pretty.

12:23.742 --> 12:25.911
Women are lining up to meet my son.

12:25.995 --> 12:27.455
Is that so?

12:27.538 --> 12:30.207
The minister
and the director of my husband's hospital

12:30.291 --> 12:33.544
both keep begging me
to introduce their daughters to him.

12:33.627 --> 12:36.714
Say that again when you have
your own wedding invitations to give out.

12:39.800 --> 12:41.218
Gosh. My legs fell asleep.

12:41.302 --> 12:43.179
And victory goes to Na Mi-suk.

12:45.431 --> 12:47.099
The wedding is only a month away.

12:47.183 --> 12:48.434
I know.

12:49.268 --> 12:50.269
It's so soon.

12:51.061 --> 12:53.063
Yahoo!

12:59.445 --> 13:02.072
We're about to land, ma'am.

13:02.156 --> 13:05.159
Could you open your window shade
and straighten your seat, please?

13:06.327 --> 13:07.328
Excuse me.

13:08.829 --> 13:09.872
Ma'am…

13:17.630 --> 13:18.756
Oh, I'm sorry.

13:18.839 --> 13:21.509
I should be the one to apologize.
I startled you.

13:21.592 --> 13:25.930
No, it's just that I was dreaming
about getting beaten up.

13:26.013 --> 13:27.223
My goodness.

13:27.306 --> 13:28.557
What a nightmare.

13:29.308 --> 13:30.518
Or it could be an omen.

13:43.113 --> 13:44.365
I've arrived.

13:47.952 --> 13:52.790
COMEBACK

13:55.042 --> 13:57.628
Where is she?

14:03.384 --> 14:04.885
What the…

14:08.931 --> 14:10.099
Bae Seok-ryu!

14:17.648 --> 14:20.359
Seeing your face makes me feel like
I'm really back, Mo-eum.

14:20.442 --> 14:21.277
You.

14:21.360 --> 14:24.530
Do you know how startled I was
when you said you were at the airport?

14:24.613 --> 14:26.198
I didn't even get to wash up!

14:26.282 --> 14:27.533
I can see that.

14:27.616 --> 14:30.911
Did you miss me so much
to rush over with soot on your face?

14:30.995 --> 14:32.288
Good grief.

14:32.371 --> 14:34.832
You've become so slimy
after all those years in the US.

14:34.915 --> 14:36.041
I know.

14:36.125 --> 14:39.211
I felt it was over the top
even as I was saying it.

14:39.295 --> 14:41.839
Still, it's been years
since we've seen each other.

14:41.922 --> 14:43.799
Don't pretend you're not happy to see me.

14:46.677 --> 14:47.678
Give me a hug.

14:47.761 --> 14:49.054
Come on.

14:59.857 --> 15:00.858
A thief.

15:01.567 --> 15:02.693
She stole my luggage!

15:15.372 --> 15:16.540
What the…

15:18.042 --> 15:21.086
Warn me before you roll up the window.

15:21.170 --> 15:22.379
I almost hurt myself.

15:22.463 --> 15:25.674
I'm teaching you
to be cautious at all times.

15:26.216 --> 15:28.260
Sticking your head out like that
is dangerous.

15:29.553 --> 15:31.555
You sounded like
a real paramedic just now.

15:31.639 --> 15:33.223
That's because I really am.

15:33.307 --> 15:34.391
Exactly.

15:36.518 --> 15:39.730
Where's the girl I used to know
who'd jump off fences wearing a cape?

15:39.813 --> 15:41.065
I liked that girl.

15:41.148 --> 15:44.944
It's thanks to kids like that
that I get a paycheck.

15:45.027 --> 15:46.862
What was I thinking back then?

15:48.530 --> 15:49.615
Were you near a fire?

15:50.491 --> 15:53.953
Yes. Paramedics accompany
firefighters to the site.

15:54.036 --> 15:55.287
No one died, at least.

15:55.371 --> 15:56.538
That's good.

15:57.164 --> 15:58.624
By the way,

15:58.707 --> 16:00.250
why are you so skinny?

16:01.043 --> 16:04.338
Are you losing weight
for your wedding day?

16:04.421 --> 16:05.422
I'm killing it, right?

16:06.006 --> 16:07.174
This jawline could cut you.

16:07.257 --> 16:10.511
Could you avoid using
dangerous words like "kill" or "cut"?

16:11.053 --> 16:12.346
It's making me antsy.

16:12.429 --> 16:13.347
Sorry.

16:13.430 --> 16:14.807
Did you call your mom?

16:15.683 --> 16:18.394
My mom didn't tell me
you were coming back home.

16:18.477 --> 16:19.645
Sure I did.

16:20.270 --> 16:22.856
Of course you did. What about Seung-hyo?

16:22.940 --> 16:24.233
He must be busy anyway.

16:24.942 --> 16:26.485
How is he anyway?

16:27.403 --> 16:28.404
He's doing good.

16:31.532 --> 16:35.703
You forgot to say my name
in your acceptance speech.

16:35.786 --> 16:36.662
I did.

16:36.745 --> 16:40.124
No, you just mentioned the company's name
and not mine!

16:40.207 --> 16:43.711
I can tell from the color of your suit
that you visited another memorial park.

16:43.794 --> 16:44.670
Yes.

16:44.753 --> 16:45.963
Did you take a compass?

16:46.046 --> 16:47.297
No.

16:47.381 --> 16:50.592
Yeah right. You can't deceive me.

16:50.676 --> 16:53.470
You're an architect,
not a feng shui master!

16:53.554 --> 16:54.805
It's part of an architect's job

16:54.888 --> 16:58.142
to learn about the cultural
and historical context of a space.

16:58.225 --> 17:00.519
Don't you know about gravesite feng shui,

17:00.602 --> 17:02.604
a long-standing traditional practice?

17:04.273 --> 17:05.774
You're absolutely right.

17:05.858 --> 17:07.109
Put that camera away.

17:07.192 --> 17:10.446
I can visit a hundred memorial parks
as long as I'm with you.

17:10.529 --> 17:12.948
If you want, I can get buried with you.

17:13.032 --> 17:14.241
No, thank you.

17:14.324 --> 17:16.160
Come on, don't be shy.

17:16.744 --> 17:17.995
I'm scared. I think she means it.

17:18.078 --> 17:19.121
Yes, me too.

17:27.504 --> 17:30.299
Hey, it's Roh Yoon-seo!

17:30.382 --> 17:31.925
Do you know her?

17:32.009 --> 17:33.135
How do you know her?

17:33.218 --> 17:34.762
I don't really know her.

17:34.845 --> 17:37.681
We met briefly
at Oblique's launching ceremony.

17:37.765 --> 17:40.309
Amazing! Let's go say hello to her!

17:40.392 --> 17:42.311
I have to go now. I'm busy.

17:42.394 --> 17:44.438
Hey, where do you think you're going?

17:44.521 --> 17:46.273
She's Roh Yoon-seo,

17:46.356 --> 17:48.567
the woman whom every young man
considers perfect!

17:48.650 --> 17:49.610
You can't leave!

17:49.693 --> 17:52.071
My idea of perfection isn't a person,
but a well-made structure.

17:52.154 --> 17:53.947
- You're going there again, aren't you?
- Of course.

17:54.031 --> 17:55.199
No, I won't let you leave

17:55.282 --> 17:58.077
until you help me get her autograph
and take a photo with her!

17:58.160 --> 18:00.329
Just go. Go on!

18:00.412 --> 18:01.497
- Hey!
- Bye.

18:01.580 --> 18:02.706
Hold on.

18:02.790 --> 18:03.916
Hello.

18:43.705 --> 18:45.624
BAE SEOK-RYU

18:52.339 --> 18:53.715
"Heungbu Sausage Stew."

18:54.758 --> 18:56.176
"Sanshin Ox Bone Soup."

18:57.344 --> 18:58.804
"Grandma Kwon's Pork Wraps."

18:58.887 --> 19:00.681
Did you forget Korean or something?

19:00.764 --> 19:02.724
Why are you reading those shop signs?

19:02.808 --> 19:05.686
The restaurant signs keep catching my eye.

19:05.769 --> 19:07.062
Oh, I see.

19:07.938 --> 19:09.565
I guess I'm hungry.

19:09.648 --> 19:10.649
Right.

19:11.608 --> 19:13.110
It's past lunchtime.

19:13.193 --> 19:15.320
Everything looks so good.

19:16.196 --> 19:18.490
"The In-Law's Fried Chicken."

19:19.199 --> 19:21.910
That one doesn't sound so appetizing.

19:21.994 --> 19:24.538
Don't be greedy and just pick one place.

19:24.621 --> 19:25.706
One place?

19:26.707 --> 19:27.749
Then…

19:35.591 --> 19:36.425
Enjoy your meal.

19:36.508 --> 19:37.509
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

19:38.177 --> 19:39.344
Hey.

19:39.428 --> 19:42.598
I bet the blood of Korean people
is redder than that of others

19:42.681 --> 19:43.724
because it's actually chili paste.

19:43.807 --> 19:46.476
What a scientific theory you have there.

19:47.060 --> 19:48.979
But I thought
we'd go to your family's place.

19:49.062 --> 19:51.773
We came here all the time
during high school.

19:52.774 --> 19:56.153
All right, let's eat these rice cakes
and talk about the good old days.

19:56.236 --> 19:57.362
Wait.

19:57.446 --> 19:59.364
We should have some sundae too.

20:00.199 --> 20:01.366
Get ready.

20:01.450 --> 20:02.826
Begin the battle.

20:03.994 --> 20:04.828
Let's eat!

20:09.750 --> 20:10.751
It's good.

20:11.835 --> 20:12.836
It's so good.

20:20.302 --> 20:21.303
It's spicy though.

20:21.386 --> 20:22.387
Really spicy.

20:23.138 --> 20:24.223
Why is it so spicy?

20:25.599 --> 20:27.726
Jeez, it looks like
I can't handle spicy food now.

20:27.809 --> 20:29.686
Drink some water. Are you okay?

20:31.438 --> 20:33.774
I guess your blood
isn't as red as it used to be.

20:33.857 --> 20:36.026
You're losing your identity as a Korean.

20:36.109 --> 20:39.029
- It's too spicy.
- All right, I know what to do.

20:39.112 --> 20:41.073
Let's wash them in water first.

20:41.156 --> 20:42.991
- What are you doing?
- Say "ah."

20:43.075 --> 20:43.909
It's okay.

20:43.992 --> 20:46.453
Come on. That's sinking too low.

20:46.536 --> 20:47.829
It's okay.

20:49.498 --> 20:51.166
- Hide!
- What?

20:53.752 --> 20:55.796
- Hello.
- Hi, what can I get you?

20:55.879 --> 20:58.131
One portion of tteokbokki, assorted fries,

20:58.215 --> 21:01.009
and sundae
with lots of steamed offals, please.

21:01.093 --> 21:02.594
- All right.
- It's Dong-jin.

21:02.678 --> 21:04.179
- Exactly.
- Looks delicious.

21:14.481 --> 21:16.191
What's the deal with them?

21:18.068 --> 21:19.194
Are they feeling sick?

21:23.198 --> 21:25.117
Your food is ready.

21:25.742 --> 21:26.868
Thank you.

21:27.953 --> 21:28.996
You can pay here.

21:29.079 --> 21:30.080
Okay.

21:33.542 --> 21:34.668
Thanks.

21:34.751 --> 21:36.837
- Goodbye.
- Enjoy your food.

21:37.462 --> 21:38.463
It looks good.

21:41.008 --> 21:43.218
- Sir!
- What's in that bag?

21:43.302 --> 21:44.720
Let go of my ear first, please.

21:45.554 --> 21:47.180
- Open it.
- Okay.

21:47.764 --> 21:49.141
This tteokbokki has 500 calories.

21:49.725 --> 21:52.477
You also have sundae,
fried seaweed rolls, and fried squid?

21:52.561 --> 21:54.104
That's 1,350 calories in total.

21:54.187 --> 21:55.230
How do you know that?

21:55.314 --> 21:57.858
Listen up.
This is your exercise regimen for today.

21:58.358 --> 22:00.360
A hundred pull-ups, a hundred push-ups,

22:00.444 --> 22:02.154
two hundred lunges and burpees, each.

22:02.237 --> 22:03.864
Then 500 squats, okay?

22:03.947 --> 22:06.700
That's so unfair.
I haven't even eaten them yet!

22:06.783 --> 22:09.286
You ate all these in your mind.

22:09.369 --> 22:10.996
Don't you want your trainer certification?

22:11.079 --> 22:12.414
What about the upcoming contest?

22:12.497 --> 22:15.417
Just the fact that
you considered eating these things

22:15.500 --> 22:16.710
is a crime, all right?

22:17.961 --> 22:19.087
Hand them over.

22:19.171 --> 22:21.423
Come on, hand them over.

22:22.007 --> 22:24.009
I'm confiscating them for your own good.

22:24.676 --> 22:26.595
The offals have protein, though.

22:27.137 --> 22:29.765
Be at the gym in five minutes. Go!

22:32.684 --> 22:34.186
That dimwit.

22:35.479 --> 22:38.148
- I told him squid has more protein.
- Is he gone?

22:39.816 --> 22:41.735
It's delicious, ma'am.

22:42.694 --> 22:44.029
- Have a good day.
- You too.

22:44.112 --> 22:45.864
- He's gone, right?
- Yes.

22:46.948 --> 22:49.826
He should be eating at Dad's diner,
not here.

22:49.910 --> 22:50.827
Hey.

22:51.828 --> 22:53.663
That's the pot calling the kettle black.

22:54.623 --> 22:55.999
Anyway, what was that?

22:56.958 --> 22:58.585
Why did you hide from your brother?

22:58.668 --> 23:01.338
You might not know
since you only have sisters,

23:01.421 --> 23:03.048
but this is what having a brother is like.

23:05.717 --> 23:07.469
Does your family not know
that you're back?

23:10.806 --> 23:11.973
Surprise.

23:13.016 --> 23:14.226
I mean,

23:15.018 --> 23:16.520
it's been a while since I came home.

23:16.603 --> 23:20.190
So I thought it would be more fun
to surprise them like this

23:21.024 --> 23:23.401
than just to walk through the front door.

23:23.485 --> 23:24.402
Right.

23:24.486 --> 23:26.488
You're nuts. So you're making
a whole production out of…

23:32.035 --> 23:34.579
Wait, "a whole production"?

23:35.747 --> 23:37.124
We might as well go all-out.

24:05.360 --> 24:06.570
Come on, let's go.

24:07.362 --> 24:10.365
We need to decorate the house
until our moms come back from hiking.

24:10.448 --> 24:11.825
Wait, Mo-eum…

24:11.908 --> 24:13.869
- What?
- Please promise me one thing.

24:14.578 --> 24:18.456
Stay with me until the end of the day,
no matter what happens.

24:18.540 --> 24:19.374
What do you mean?

24:19.457 --> 24:21.835
Even if Mount Baekdu explodes
or the Han River overflows, okay?

24:21.918 --> 24:23.795
Even if the world ends
or the dinosaurs come back!

24:23.879 --> 24:24.713
Hold on.

24:24.796 --> 24:26.381
- What I mean is--
- Hello?

24:26.965 --> 24:28.008
Yes, captain?

24:28.091 --> 24:30.260
Jae-gyeong did what?

24:31.678 --> 24:32.971
Right now?

24:33.054 --> 24:35.891
- All right. I'll be right there.
- You're leaving?

24:35.974 --> 24:38.268
- Where are you going?
- I have to go. It's an emergency.

24:38.852 --> 24:39.978
I have an emergency too.

24:40.061 --> 24:41.730
I'm going to need you later on!

24:41.813 --> 24:43.982
Then call 911 later! Bye!

24:44.065 --> 24:45.483
Hey, wait! I'm being serious!

24:45.567 --> 24:47.277
Jung Mo-eum!

24:47.360 --> 24:48.445
Hey!

24:48.528 --> 24:49.696
Bye.

24:49.779 --> 24:50.780
But…

24:52.157 --> 24:53.408
That traitor.

25:09.341 --> 25:11.551
There used to be a sauna here.

25:19.142 --> 25:19.976
CORNERSTONE

25:20.060 --> 25:23.605
THIS BUILDING WAS FUNDED BY THE GOVERNMENT
FOR THE RESIDENTS OF HYEREUNG-DONG

25:23.688 --> 25:25.774
TO COMMEMORATE THE HOSTING
OF THE OLYMPIC GAMES

25:25.857 --> 25:27.275
HYEREUNG SAUNA

25:27.859 --> 25:29.361
No!

25:29.444 --> 25:31.655
You really have to take a bath today.

25:31.738 --> 25:34.908
See? You're so grimy with dirt,
I can hardly tell you're a human brat.

25:34.991 --> 25:36.243
Well, I'm your grimy brat!

25:36.326 --> 25:37.786
You're not doing this on purpose, are you?

25:37.869 --> 25:40.163
No! I don't want to take a bath!

25:40.247 --> 25:41.456
Come on!

25:41.539 --> 25:42.916
I don't want to go inside

25:42.999 --> 25:45.252
with Bae Seok-ryu.

25:45.335 --> 25:47.212
It's okay, Seung-hyo.

25:47.295 --> 25:49.130
HYEREUNG SAUNA

25:49.214 --> 25:51.216
- Oh, come on.
- No!

25:51.299 --> 25:52.926
SAUNA OPEN

25:53.009 --> 25:55.804
WOMEN'S BATH

26:02.602 --> 26:04.604
Our mothers were so cruel.

26:05.981 --> 26:09.651
How could they make us share a bath?

26:11.528 --> 26:13.655
It was a violation of our rights.

26:15.740 --> 26:18.201
I used to hate going to the sauna,

26:18.285 --> 26:19.536
but it's a shame it's gone.

26:22.455 --> 26:23.915
What is this place anyway?

26:24.666 --> 26:25.750
There's no sign.

26:25.834 --> 26:26.960
No front door either.

26:32.257 --> 26:33.091
Who are you?

26:53.153 --> 26:54.154
Bae Seok-ryu?

26:56.740 --> 26:57.741
Choisseung?

27:04.164 --> 27:06.166
What are you doing here?

27:06.249 --> 27:07.375
That's my line.

27:07.876 --> 27:08.918
What's up with you?

27:09.586 --> 27:10.670
None of your business.

27:11.254 --> 27:12.964
You're stepping on my land.

27:13.798 --> 27:16.968
Don't make me laugh. This is your land?

27:19.971 --> 27:20.847
Wait, is it?

27:21.431 --> 27:22.891
It is, so go away.

27:36.321 --> 27:38.573
- I do dancesport.
- Your old age is showing.

27:45.038 --> 27:46.039
What the heck?

27:49.876 --> 27:51.878
- What are you doing?
- I can't talk right now.

27:51.961 --> 27:53.129
Just help me out, okay?

27:53.213 --> 27:54.964
What are you going on about?

27:55.048 --> 27:57.175
Help me out just this once.

27:57.258 --> 28:00.220
Just pretend I'm a discarded box, okay?

28:00.303 --> 28:02.555
Don't tell anyone you saw me.

28:03.848 --> 28:04.891
Got it?

28:06.142 --> 28:07.811
Whatever. Get out.

28:08.395 --> 28:10.105
- I said, get out.
- I don't believe you.

28:11.398 --> 28:12.399
You want proof?

28:13.400 --> 28:14.484
- Look at her.
- Hey.

28:14.984 --> 28:16.903
Hey, stop that!

28:16.986 --> 28:18.863
- That's enough!
- Gosh, how embarrassing.

28:18.947 --> 28:20.115
One, two!

28:20.198 --> 28:23.701
What's this luggage doing here
in the middle of the road?

28:23.785 --> 28:25.328
- Seung-hyo.
- Mom.

28:26.913 --> 28:28.081
Give me a hug.

28:28.164 --> 28:30.041
Oh my.

28:30.125 --> 28:32.377
- It's been a while, Seung-hyo.
- You're here.

28:32.460 --> 28:34.712
- You're as handsome as always.
- He is.

28:34.796 --> 28:37.048
I'm In-suk. Do you remember me?

28:37.132 --> 28:38.425
Of course. How have you been?

28:38.508 --> 28:40.051
My goodness!

28:40.135 --> 28:42.095
- Hello.
- What are you doing here?

28:42.178 --> 28:43.388
- Hello.
- Hi.

28:43.471 --> 28:45.098
- Why aren't you at the diner?
- What?

28:45.181 --> 28:46.349
Where are you sneaking off to?

28:46.850 --> 28:48.309
Why would I be sneaking?

28:48.393 --> 28:50.770
Is that any way to talk
to your beloved husband?

28:50.854 --> 28:51.813
Wanna try that again?

28:51.896 --> 28:53.189
I just went to the market.

28:54.899 --> 28:57.360
Hey, Seung-hyo! Here, have one.

28:57.986 --> 28:59.529
- Thank you.
- It's good to see you.

28:59.612 --> 29:00.655
Thank you.

29:02.073 --> 29:04.701
You should've called ahead
to say you were coming home.

29:06.161 --> 29:07.954
I came to receive some furniture today.

29:08.037 --> 29:09.622
- I apologize for not letting you know.
- I see.

29:10.957 --> 29:12.250
I understand.

29:13.626 --> 29:15.503
Your firm opens next week,
so you must be busy.

29:15.587 --> 29:18.631
I invited a lot of guests
for the opening party.

29:18.715 --> 29:20.967
- About that--
- So you're saying that this building

29:21.050 --> 29:22.177
is your new office?

29:22.260 --> 29:24.804
- Yes.
- That's impressive, Seung-hyo.

29:24.888 --> 29:25.930
- Thank you.
- Seung-hyo.

29:26.514 --> 29:28.475
- Is this your luggage?
- What? No.

29:29.184 --> 29:30.810
- Really?
- This was just here?

29:30.894 --> 29:33.521
- We should take it to the police.
- We should.

29:34.773 --> 29:36.107
- Let's do it.
- Let me see.

29:36.191 --> 29:37.442
It says something here.

29:37.525 --> 29:39.027
It's in English.

29:39.110 --> 29:40.236
Hold on. It is mine.

29:41.112 --> 29:42.614
It's definitely mine.

29:42.697 --> 29:45.408
Seung-hyo has the same taste as me.

29:46.034 --> 29:48.411
- I suppose.
- Pink is a man's color, you know.

29:48.495 --> 29:50.622
- Right.
- You should take better care of it.

29:50.705 --> 29:53.166
What if you lost it? Here you go.

29:53.792 --> 29:54.793
I'll do it.

29:56.294 --> 29:57.337
Seung-hyo.

29:57.420 --> 29:59.380
Did you eat the beans I sent you?

29:59.464 --> 30:02.425
- Did you eat everything?
- Actually, not yet.

30:02.509 --> 30:04.719
I've been too busy to eat at home.

30:05.595 --> 30:07.555
You need to have healthier eating habits!

30:07.639 --> 30:09.891
You want me to come over
and check your fridge?

30:09.974 --> 30:12.727
I'm sorry. I'll give you an apple
as an apology.

30:13.311 --> 30:14.229
An apology?

30:14.771 --> 30:16.856
I'm only eating beans from today onward.

30:17.607 --> 30:21.194
What are you guarding this box for anyway?
What's in it?

30:21.277 --> 30:22.195
I don't know.

30:22.278 --> 30:24.697
I mean, it can't be a person, can it?

30:26.366 --> 30:27.909
Are you hiding something precious?

30:27.992 --> 30:29.077
Of course not.

30:29.661 --> 30:30.954
It has nothing of value.

30:31.955 --> 30:32.789
I should throw it out.

30:33.665 --> 30:35.500
Really? Then we'll throw it out for you.

30:35.583 --> 30:38.002
- Honey.
- Yes, I can carry it.

30:38.086 --> 30:39.963
You can sell a box like this for money.

30:40.046 --> 30:41.422
Hold on.

30:41.506 --> 30:45.802
Now that I think about it,
I still need it to put all my trash in.

30:45.885 --> 30:46.845
I'll throw it out after that.

30:46.928 --> 30:49.389
Maybe there is
something of value after all.

30:49.472 --> 30:51.182
- Really?
- Okay.

30:51.266 --> 30:53.226
Tell me when you plan to throw it out.

30:53.309 --> 30:54.185
Okay.

30:55.061 --> 30:56.312
Seung-hyo.

30:56.813 --> 30:57.897
Don't forget the beans.

30:57.981 --> 30:59.274
Yes, ma'am.

30:59.357 --> 31:00.733
You should cook it better.

31:00.817 --> 31:01.818
Let's go.

31:01.901 --> 31:03.194
- Bye!
- Goodbye!

31:03.278 --> 31:04.821
- Goodbye.
- Have a good day!

31:06.322 --> 31:07.907
I'll be going too, Seung-hyo.

31:07.991 --> 31:09.284
All right. Goodbye.

31:09.367 --> 31:10.660
- See you later.
- Yes.

31:10.743 --> 31:11.953
Bye.

31:20.712 --> 31:22.005
Are they all gone?

31:23.298 --> 31:24.132
I'm coming out.

31:32.015 --> 31:33.016
Let me out.

31:33.600 --> 31:35.727
Why are you hiding from your mom?

31:36.978 --> 31:38.479
Let me out! It's stuffy in here!

31:39.230 --> 31:40.982
It's just very strange.

31:41.065 --> 31:43.693
I thought you were
supposed to be in the US.

31:47.238 --> 31:48.740
Did you get into trouble?

31:50.033 --> 31:52.035
I have other ways of getting out.

31:52.619 --> 31:53.786
Jeez.

31:55.914 --> 31:57.415
You tore the box?

31:59.208 --> 32:00.418
I can tear you apart too.

32:01.711 --> 32:02.754
Aunt Mi-suk!

32:04.464 --> 32:05.298
Just kidding.

32:09.260 --> 32:10.929
I'm going to end you!

32:11.888 --> 32:13.890
Is that any way to talk to your savior?

32:15.058 --> 32:17.936
So this is your new office?

32:18.019 --> 32:18.853
It kind of sucks.

32:19.479 --> 32:21.064
- It's full of bucks though.
- Whatever.

32:21.898 --> 32:24.901
Then why don't you save me one more time?

32:24.984 --> 32:25.818
What?

32:25.902 --> 32:27.070
Let me use your bathroom.

32:27.862 --> 32:30.156
Don't mark it as your territory.

32:30.239 --> 32:31.616
You can't go in there!

32:33.159 --> 32:34.285
Jeez.

32:40.041 --> 32:43.044
Go straight and turn left there.
That's the front door.

32:43.127 --> 32:44.170
Goodbye.

32:44.253 --> 32:45.922
It's actually not that bad.

32:46.798 --> 32:48.383
Just follow the recommended route.

32:49.217 --> 32:51.260
Hey, what are these?

32:51.344 --> 32:52.178
Millstones?

32:53.638 --> 32:55.348
They're stepping stones.

32:56.683 --> 32:58.643
Keep your dirty hands off of them!

33:01.437 --> 33:02.939
Are you doing this on purpose?

33:05.608 --> 33:07.276
Does this place have bad feng shui?

33:07.360 --> 33:09.237
Or are you my bad luck?

33:09.320 --> 33:12.407
You know you're kind of mean, don't you?

33:12.490 --> 33:14.409
You don't know you're immature, do you?

33:15.952 --> 33:17.829
I don't like this at all.

33:17.912 --> 33:19.789
At least you were cute
when you were little.

33:20.373 --> 33:22.083
You weren't cute
even when you were little.

33:22.709 --> 33:24.877
You little…

33:25.378 --> 33:26.587
Look at this.

33:27.088 --> 33:28.965
You immediately start throwing punches.

33:29.048 --> 33:33.219
I tell you, you're closer to a beast
than a human being.

33:34.095 --> 33:35.430
Your fiancé must be a saint.

33:36.264 --> 33:37.223
What?

33:37.306 --> 33:38.933
Aunt Mi-suk gave me
your wedding invitation.

33:39.517 --> 33:41.436
She offered to buy my plane ticket,

33:41.519 --> 33:43.896
but I think I'll be too busy to make it.

33:46.482 --> 33:48.484
Congratulations on your marriage.

33:49.485 --> 33:50.486
Thanks.

33:52.113 --> 33:53.948
By the way, where's your office?

33:55.783 --> 33:56.993
Aren't you going to leave?

33:59.120 --> 33:59.954
It's over there, isn't it?

34:01.456 --> 34:03.875
Please just leave!

34:03.958 --> 34:06.419
Just go, please.
Why are you going upstairs?

34:06.502 --> 34:09.505
Hey, come on! Get out of there.

34:09.589 --> 34:11.382
Why would you come in here?

34:11.466 --> 34:14.135
Your office is huge.

34:15.178 --> 34:16.971
Just go home, okay?

34:18.723 --> 34:20.683
That's an impressive ceiling.

34:22.393 --> 34:23.895
I guess you have eyes, after all.

34:25.813 --> 34:28.316
I referred to the ceiling designs
of the Goguryeo mural tombs.

34:28.399 --> 34:30.985
You mean like the Twin Column Tomb
or the Tomb of the Dancers?

34:31.069 --> 34:31.903
Exactly.

34:32.862 --> 34:34.447
It's a ceiling
with triangles in each corner,

34:34.530 --> 34:36.282
the most common type of the era.

34:37.158 --> 34:38.409
It holds the principles of

34:38.493 --> 34:41.287
"the sky is round
and the earth is square."

34:41.370 --> 34:42.580
In other words,

34:43.331 --> 34:45.958
you designed your office like a tomb.
What a weirdo.

34:46.042 --> 34:47.627
What? A "weirdo"?

34:49.170 --> 34:50.254
Whatever.

34:51.380 --> 34:54.300
Of course, someone as crude as you
wouldn't understand my art,

34:54.383 --> 34:56.594
which reinterprets
our ancestors' timeless wisdom

34:56.677 --> 34:58.429
with modern sensibilities--

35:10.483 --> 35:12.527
For crying out loud.

35:14.153 --> 35:15.071
Are you okay?

35:17.532 --> 35:19.992
Do I look okay to you?

35:21.119 --> 35:22.829
I can't believe you crawled out alone.

35:23.329 --> 35:26.290
I have a very strong attachment to life.

35:28.459 --> 35:30.419
What was it that fell anyway?

35:32.505 --> 35:35.591
This thing is heavy!

35:35.675 --> 35:38.219
Did you think it'd be
as light as a feather?

35:39.971 --> 35:40.972
Did you hurt yourself?

35:41.597 --> 35:42.557
Let me see.

35:42.640 --> 35:44.100
What are you doing?

35:44.183 --> 35:45.852
Do you have eyes in the back of your head?

35:45.935 --> 35:47.728
If you don't, just stay still.

35:48.521 --> 35:49.814
I knew this would happen.

35:49.897 --> 35:52.859
I always end up getting hurt
when I'm with you.

35:52.942 --> 35:54.902
Be quiet and stay still.

35:56.696 --> 35:58.906
You're completely fine.
Nothing to worry about.

35:58.990 --> 36:00.950
But it might leave a bruise…

36:04.912 --> 36:08.040
What did you just say? Say it again!

36:10.376 --> 36:11.586
Stop it!

36:11.669 --> 36:12.670
Don't!

36:12.753 --> 36:13.796
Let me go!

36:24.056 --> 36:25.558
You still have this scar.

36:27.727 --> 36:29.187
I told you, didn't I?

36:29.270 --> 36:33.524
My body is bruised and battered
from everything you put me through.

36:34.108 --> 36:35.568
You're exaggerating.

36:35.651 --> 36:37.236
I don't expect you to apologize.

36:37.904 --> 36:40.865
I just want you to leave now. Please.

36:40.948 --> 36:44.327
Hey, I didn't want to spend
my first day back with you either.

36:44.410 --> 36:47.163
- But something unexpected came up--
- Hey, Seok-ryu.

36:47.246 --> 36:50.041
I couldn't care less
about what you did or didn't do.

36:51.167 --> 36:52.001
I see.

36:52.668 --> 36:55.004
Sorry for inconveniencing you.

36:56.464 --> 36:57.590
But I know one thing.

36:59.634 --> 37:02.595
Knowing Aunt Mi-suk, putting it off
wouldn't do you any favors.

37:02.678 --> 37:05.264
Things are going to escalate
the longer you put it off.

37:05.348 --> 37:07.266
She'll spend a whole day
not talking to you

37:07.350 --> 37:08.893
for what could've been resolved
in 30 minutes.

37:08.976 --> 37:12.230
So stop dawdling
and just get it over with.

37:12.313 --> 37:14.607
You're so annoying when you're right.

37:14.690 --> 37:17.610
You're so pathetic
when you get in trouble.

37:19.612 --> 37:20.613
That's it.

37:21.322 --> 37:22.615
Let me hit you just once.

37:23.157 --> 37:23.991
I think

37:24.992 --> 37:26.619
this cost 17 million won.

37:26.702 --> 37:28.120
Not 1,700 won?

37:28.204 --> 37:30.665
A designer friend of mine gave it to me.

37:30.748 --> 37:33.251
If it's broken,
I should claim for damages--

37:33.334 --> 37:34.543
Let me see.

37:37.213 --> 37:38.631
It's not broken. It's fine.

37:39.131 --> 37:41.550
What an expensive chunk of metal.

37:43.511 --> 37:45.721
Look. I gave it a rub so it shines better.

37:45.805 --> 37:46.973
It's so shiny now.

37:47.056 --> 37:48.349
It's totally fine, right?

37:48.432 --> 37:49.642
It's as good as new.

37:49.725 --> 37:51.644
I'll just carefully put it back here.

37:51.727 --> 37:52.812
Don't bother.

37:52.895 --> 37:55.648
There, all done!
It looks even better than before.

37:55.731 --> 37:57.358
- Just go.
- It looks so perfect.

37:57.441 --> 38:00.069
HYEREUNG 911 SAFETY CENTER

38:04.323 --> 38:05.324
Hey.

38:06.075 --> 38:08.869
How could you call me back
after I'd gone home for the day?

38:08.953 --> 38:10.371
I'm not even on this team.

38:10.454 --> 38:11.789
I had no choice.

38:11.872 --> 38:13.833
The newbie got seriously carsick.

38:13.916 --> 38:17.378
I told you
Captain Song should drive slower.

38:17.461 --> 38:21.674
You're the only one
who can bear to be in the car with him.

38:21.757 --> 38:23.009
Who would've guessed

38:23.092 --> 38:25.511
that a good paramedic
is one who doesn't get carsick?

38:26.637 --> 38:27.638
I'm leaving.

38:28.514 --> 38:29.515
Emergency dispatch.

38:30.641 --> 38:35.146
911 AMBULANCE

38:47.575 --> 38:48.576
Sir.

38:49.869 --> 38:51.412
I'm a paramedic.

38:52.705 --> 38:53.581
Are you okay?

38:53.664 --> 38:54.999
Can you hear me?

38:55.082 --> 38:58.210
What? Who called 911?

38:58.294 --> 38:59.545
Who was it?

39:00.379 --> 39:01.464
Jeez.

39:01.547 --> 39:04.300
We got a call that you collapsed
with a cut on your forehead.

39:04.383 --> 39:06.385
We'll take you to the hospital.

39:06.469 --> 39:08.054
How did you get hurt?

39:08.137 --> 39:10.973
I just fell from a chair.

39:11.057 --> 39:13.100
It's fine. I don't need a doctor.

39:13.184 --> 39:14.518
Yes, you do.

39:14.602 --> 39:15.728
It could be superficial,

39:15.811 --> 39:17.855
but we can't rule out concussion.

39:17.938 --> 39:19.190
You should get checked out.

39:19.273 --> 39:20.316
Get lost.

39:20.399 --> 39:21.692
I said get lost.

39:23.152 --> 39:27.198
Jeez, I'm hungry.
When is my mother getting here?

39:27.281 --> 39:29.742
- For crying out loud.
- Sir.

39:29.825 --> 39:30.826
Sir.

39:31.911 --> 39:33.287
Do you have diabetes?

39:35.414 --> 39:36.832
You shouldn't have drunk this much.

39:36.916 --> 39:38.626
I told you to get lost.

39:38.709 --> 39:39.752
Careful.

39:39.835 --> 39:42.671
Come on, Captain Jung.
Let's just call the police.

39:42.755 --> 39:44.882
- Let me check your blood sugar level.
- Why you…

39:44.965 --> 39:45.966
I said no!

39:46.050 --> 39:47.676
I'm not going to the hospital!

39:47.760 --> 39:49.845
Stop bothering me and get lost!

39:49.929 --> 39:51.514
Don't curse at me.

39:51.597 --> 39:53.557
Do you see this camera I'm wearing?

39:53.641 --> 39:56.811
I have no choice but to film your face
if you keep acting like this.

39:56.894 --> 39:59.563
I told you to get lost
and stop bothering me.

39:59.647 --> 40:00.815
Why would you film me?

40:01.357 --> 40:03.275
Who do you think you are to do that?

40:05.486 --> 40:06.529
Get back, Mo-eum.

40:06.612 --> 40:08.030
Sir.

40:08.114 --> 40:09.698
Put down that bottle, please.

40:09.782 --> 40:11.200
And who the hell are you?

40:11.283 --> 40:12.159
I'm just a civilian.

40:12.243 --> 40:14.203
Everyone, please stay out of this.

40:14.286 --> 40:15.371
We'll deal with it.

40:15.454 --> 40:17.873
I wanted to help out
because the situation looked dangerous.

40:17.957 --> 40:19.500
Why? Because I'm a woman?

40:19.583 --> 40:20.626
No,

40:20.709 --> 40:22.461
because I'm a red belt in taekwondo.

40:23.129 --> 40:25.506
- What?
- I'm sorry, sir!

40:26.132 --> 40:27.466
Hold on!

40:29.593 --> 40:31.595
What's the deal with him?

40:31.679 --> 40:32.513
What the…

40:42.064 --> 40:43.107
I'm a black belt.

40:43.190 --> 40:45.317
Can you treat him, please?

40:46.694 --> 40:47.987
Are you okay, sir?

40:48.654 --> 40:49.488
Good grief.

40:49.572 --> 40:50.656
What?

40:50.739 --> 40:52.074
Let me just check your blood.

40:52.158 --> 40:53.909
Oh, all right.

40:54.827 --> 40:55.828
It's going to sting.

40:55.911 --> 40:57.246
- Okay.
- Give me your hand.

40:58.789 --> 41:01.083
Why did you drink so much?

41:25.483 --> 41:28.903
It's so noisy. Don't walk so close to me.

41:29.487 --> 41:32.656
You're the one who's following me.

41:33.657 --> 41:36.744
Do you think I'm following you?

41:36.827 --> 41:38.537
You might have forgotten,

41:38.621 --> 41:40.456
but our parents live
right next to each other.

41:40.539 --> 41:41.665
I'm just going home.

41:41.749 --> 41:44.752
Just take another road. Go on.

41:44.835 --> 41:45.836
This is the quickest.

41:46.420 --> 41:47.671
For crying out loud.

41:58.015 --> 42:00.059
Are you craving fried chicken right now?

42:00.142 --> 42:01.101
THE IN-LAW'S FRIED CHICKEN

42:01.185 --> 42:04.313
I feel sorry for you. I really do.

42:04.396 --> 42:09.527
Do you think I could ask
to borrow that helmet right there?

42:09.610 --> 42:11.445
You think they'd lend it to me?

42:12.154 --> 42:12.988
What?

42:13.072 --> 42:14.865
I need something
to protect me from my mom.

42:14.949 --> 42:15.950
She'll crack my melon.

42:16.033 --> 42:19.328
You could've picked a more normal word
like "head" or even "skull."

42:19.411 --> 42:23.874
There aren't any helmet shops nearby,
are there?

42:23.958 --> 42:26.001
This lunatic is actually being serious.

42:33.717 --> 42:34.593
What are you doing?

42:38.806 --> 42:40.891
What are you doing
in the middle of the street?

42:43.143 --> 42:44.478
Hold this.

42:47.314 --> 42:48.357
Hey.

42:48.440 --> 42:49.900
You're driving me nuts.

42:55.072 --> 42:58.659
I guess I underestimated you.

43:02.913 --> 43:03.998
You're insane.

43:19.597 --> 43:21.098
You look like a blowfish.

43:21.181 --> 43:23.517
It's only natural to puff up one's body

43:23.601 --> 43:25.144
when faced with incredible danger.

43:26.729 --> 43:27.855
Come on, hit me.

43:27.938 --> 43:29.565
What are you saying?

43:29.648 --> 43:32.610
Just hit me. I need to see
if I'm protected enough.

43:32.693 --> 43:35.613
Why didn't you just buy
a bulletproof vest in the US?

43:36.196 --> 43:37.865
I really should've.

43:38.574 --> 43:40.534
Should I go back and buy one?

43:41.285 --> 43:43.203
Considering the time and money
you'd have to spend,

43:43.787 --> 43:45.372
just get it over with right now.

43:48.834 --> 43:51.128
Hey, do you want to
spend the night with me?

43:51.712 --> 43:52.713
What the hell are you on about?

43:52.796 --> 43:53.922
Stay with me.

43:54.006 --> 43:54.923
Stop fooling around.

43:55.007 --> 43:57.676
I'm not asking for much.
Just stay by my side, okay?

43:57.760 --> 43:59.428
Go away! You're scaring me.

43:59.511 --> 44:01.263
I'm the one who's scared.

44:02.264 --> 44:04.516
I really screwed up, Seung-hyo.

44:05.517 --> 44:08.562
I came home to just tell my mom
and get it over with,

44:09.480 --> 44:12.149
but now I can't bear to face her.

44:13.025 --> 44:14.693
What is it? What did you do?

44:17.363 --> 44:18.530
I have to know what it is

44:18.614 --> 44:21.659
if I'm going to help you
decide what to do about it.

44:21.742 --> 44:22.576
Well…

44:23.869 --> 44:24.870
The thing is…

44:26.830 --> 44:27.665
I…

44:29.917 --> 44:30.918
called it off.

44:31.502 --> 44:32.336
What?

44:32.836 --> 44:33.796
I said…

44:35.005 --> 44:35.881
I'm not getting married.

44:35.964 --> 44:37.466
Speak up, will you?

44:37.549 --> 44:39.593
I said I broke off my engagement!

44:44.056 --> 44:44.890
Aunt Mi-suk.

44:46.100 --> 44:49.645
Hey, you can't fool me twice
with that trick.

44:50.437 --> 44:52.773
What did you just say?

45:09.873 --> 45:10.916
Seok-ryu.

45:11.583 --> 45:13.919
What did you say? Say it again.

45:14.503 --> 45:15.337
Mom.

45:16.797 --> 45:19.091
I must have heard it wrong, right?

45:19.174 --> 45:20.676
Right.

45:20.759 --> 45:21.802
Mom!

45:21.885 --> 45:23.387
- Oh my.
- How have you been?

45:23.470 --> 45:26.890
You must be surprised to see me
out of the blue.

45:27.474 --> 45:28.725
You're still so beautiful.

45:28.809 --> 45:32.354
I'm actually kind of confused
because of jet lag, you know?

45:32.438 --> 45:35.274
The reason I'm back in Korea is…

45:35.357 --> 45:36.191
Yes?

45:37.568 --> 45:38.402
It's…

45:39.069 --> 45:40.779
to tell you
that I broke off my engagement.

45:42.406 --> 45:43.282
Oh my god!

45:47.870 --> 45:49.079
- Dad!
- Geun-sik!

45:49.163 --> 45:50.289
Dad!

45:50.372 --> 45:51.415
Move out of the way.

45:54.376 --> 45:55.627
He must have had a shock.

45:56.962 --> 45:58.046
Goodness!

45:59.173 --> 46:01.091
Are you all right, Geun-sik?

46:01.175 --> 46:02.217
I just had a bad dream.

46:03.218 --> 46:05.220
- I thought Seok-ryu said…
- Are you okay, Dad?

46:05.304 --> 46:06.472
Seok-ryu!

46:07.055 --> 46:08.432
It wasn't a dream?

46:08.515 --> 46:12.227
No, this has to be a dream!
Just a bad dream!

46:12.311 --> 46:13.437
Seok-ryu.

46:13.520 --> 46:16.148
What did you say? You did what?

46:17.441 --> 46:18.984
I broke off my engagement.

46:19.860 --> 46:20.986
I canceled everything.

46:21.612 --> 46:23.113
Everyone in the US knows already.

46:23.197 --> 46:24.615
You're out of your mind.

46:25.115 --> 46:26.867
You're completely nuts.

46:26.950 --> 46:27.951
I'm totally fine.

46:28.035 --> 46:30.412
How could you call your own daughter nuts?

46:30.496 --> 46:31.663
I'm calling it as I see it!

46:31.747 --> 46:35.334
Only a nutjob would pull a stunt like this
a month before the wedding!

46:36.126 --> 46:37.294
Come here.

46:37.377 --> 46:38.545
Aunt Mi-suk!

46:38.629 --> 46:40.714
Use your words, please.

46:40.797 --> 46:43.425
- No violence.
- That's right, Mom. Hear me out.

46:43.509 --> 46:45.135
There's a saying in the US.

46:45.219 --> 46:47.930
"There are three types of people
who get married."

46:48.013 --> 46:51.391
"The dumb, the poor, and the masochist."

46:51.475 --> 46:52.935
Why you… Get over here.

46:53.018 --> 46:54.686
Wait, I have more.

46:54.770 --> 46:56.772
I have one more thing to say.

46:56.855 --> 46:58.524
There's another saying that goes,

46:58.607 --> 47:03.028
"Marriage is leaving a festival
before it begins."

47:03.111 --> 47:04.321
Are you nuts?

47:04.404 --> 47:06.448
What in the world happened?

47:06.532 --> 47:08.408
You sounded so happy

47:08.492 --> 47:10.118
- the last time we talked!
- Stop it.

47:12.704 --> 47:14.248
Don't tell me that my son…

47:14.331 --> 47:16.208
No, he's not my son-in-law anymore.

47:16.917 --> 47:19.461
Did that jerk Song Hyeon-jun call it off?

47:20.087 --> 47:22.047
That dirtbag!

47:22.130 --> 47:24.550
Honey, buy us
two plane tickets right away.

47:24.633 --> 47:26.677
- Okay.
- I'll tear him to pieces!

47:26.760 --> 47:28.053
It's not his fault.

47:28.720 --> 47:30.055
Do you have no pride?

47:30.639 --> 47:32.140
Are you seriously defending him?

47:32.224 --> 47:34.893
It wasn't his fault. It was mine.

47:34.977 --> 47:36.019
That makes no sense.

47:36.812 --> 47:38.355
What could you have possibly…

47:40.774 --> 47:41.817
Did you…

47:44.945 --> 47:46.071
cheat on him?

47:50.951 --> 47:52.119
Goodness.

47:52.202 --> 47:54.371
Dear me.

47:55.747 --> 47:57.708
Be careful.

47:58.333 --> 47:59.376
Now,

47:59.459 --> 48:01.003
breathe in deeply.

48:01.086 --> 48:02.546
You might start hyperventilating.

48:02.629 --> 48:04.006
I need CPR.

48:04.089 --> 48:05.632
You crazy brat!

48:05.716 --> 48:07.175
I can't believe you!

48:07.759 --> 48:11.096
- Even I never cheated on anyone,
- Mi-suk!

48:11.179 --> 48:13.056
with a pathetic husband like that!

48:13.140 --> 48:15.475
So how could you do
such an unthinkable thing?

48:15.559 --> 48:17.686
I've had it up to here with you!
I'll end you!

48:17.769 --> 48:20.772
- Aunt Mi-suk!
- You don't have to talk to me like that.

48:20.856 --> 48:24.651
Do you want me to be an unfilial daughter
who dies before her parents?

48:24.735 --> 48:25.777
- Hey.
- What about now?

48:25.861 --> 48:27.613
As if you're a filial daughter now!

48:27.696 --> 48:30.532
- Mi-suk! Stop!
- Auntie! Hold on!

48:30.616 --> 48:33.035
- Let's talk it out like civilized people.
- That's right!

48:33.118 --> 48:35.162
Let's be civilized.
You're being too violent.

48:35.245 --> 48:36.204
Also, I'm a grownup.

48:36.288 --> 48:39.291
You can't just
discipline me like that anymore!

48:39.374 --> 48:41.585
I'll treat you like a grownup
when you act like one!

48:41.668 --> 48:43.295
Come over here, you brat!

48:43.378 --> 48:45.464
- Aunt Mi-suk!
- What are you doing?

48:45.547 --> 48:47.674
Stop hitting me and hit her instead!

48:47.758 --> 48:49.051
That's right!

48:49.635 --> 48:51.261
Why are you hitting my son?

48:51.345 --> 48:54.056
He's taking all the blows
for your daughter!

48:55.223 --> 48:57.643
He's so cruel and ruthless.

48:57.726 --> 48:59.978
He really made me do all the push-ups.

49:00.062 --> 49:01.730
- Come here, you brat!
- Hey!

49:01.813 --> 49:03.148
What's with the ruckus?

49:03.231 --> 49:05.317
- You should go.
- Is someone fighting?

49:05.400 --> 49:09.196
Why do you keep calling me "brat"
instead of the name you gave me?

49:09.279 --> 49:10.572
That's your issue?

49:10.656 --> 49:12.866
How about I call you "bastard" instead?

49:13.700 --> 49:15.744
- I think I prefer "brat."
- Hey, you…

49:15.827 --> 49:17.162
Are you making fun of me?

49:17.245 --> 49:19.373
Aunt Mi-suk! Stop!

49:19.456 --> 49:21.249
Don't hit me there!

49:21.333 --> 49:22.668
Hey!

49:23.794 --> 49:25.837
Are you trying to castrate my son?

49:25.921 --> 49:27.297
I've had enough.

49:27.381 --> 49:29.341
Let me go! Stop it!

49:29.424 --> 49:30.842
- Honey.
- Out of my way!

49:30.926 --> 49:31.927
Don't do this.

49:33.428 --> 49:34.429
Uncle Geun-sik.

49:37.057 --> 49:38.058
Honey, please!

49:39.434 --> 49:40.727
Stop hitting her, okay?

49:41.311 --> 49:44.231
You haven't even heard
Seok-ryu's side of the story yet.

49:44.314 --> 49:47.734
She wouldn't do something like that
for no reason!

49:49.152 --> 49:50.237
Dad.

49:51.405 --> 49:53.448
Oh, my daughter.

49:53.532 --> 49:54.825
It's okay.

49:55.659 --> 49:58.036
She basically raised herself
without our help!

49:58.120 --> 50:01.039
So she must have had a reason
for doing whatever she did!

50:08.004 --> 50:09.005
Fine, tell me.

50:10.006 --> 50:10.882
Let's hear it.

50:11.717 --> 50:13.844
Will you stop hitting me if I tell you?

50:14.553 --> 50:15.429
Fine.

50:16.096 --> 50:18.890
Will you really listen to
everything I have to say?

50:18.974 --> 50:19.850
Yes.

50:20.600 --> 50:21.893
I'll listen.

50:22.644 --> 50:23.895
Are you sure?

50:23.979 --> 50:25.731
- I said yes.
- She said yes.

50:26.773 --> 50:27.774
Mom.

50:29.693 --> 50:31.570
I also quit my work.

50:32.279 --> 50:33.280
I'm unemployed now.

50:39.494 --> 50:40.579
No way.

50:40.662 --> 50:41.830
So you're… what?

50:45.709 --> 50:47.002
- Dad!
- Geun-sik!

50:50.589 --> 50:52.299
Is he okay?

50:52.382 --> 50:53.800
Dong-jin!

50:53.884 --> 50:55.844
- What is it?
- I'm just so…

50:55.927 --> 50:56.762
You little…

50:57.512 --> 50:58.805
You hopeless brat!

51:00.140 --> 51:01.141
You quit your job

51:02.058 --> 51:03.018
on top of all that?

51:03.101 --> 51:04.227
You're insane!

51:04.311 --> 51:05.854
- Goodness, Mi-suk!
- Come here!

51:05.937 --> 51:06.897
Seok-ryu!

51:06.980 --> 51:08.982
- You said you'd hear me out!
- You're hitting Seung-hyo!

51:09.065 --> 51:11.860
- You're hitting my son!
- This is too ridiculous!

51:11.943 --> 51:13.987
- You worked so hard to get there!
- Stop it!

51:14.070 --> 51:15.363
- You had such a good job.
- Stop!

51:15.447 --> 51:17.073
- Why would you quit?
- Hey!

51:17.157 --> 51:18.825
- You little brat!
- Stop it.

51:18.909 --> 51:20.285
- I can't believe…
- It hurts!

51:20.368 --> 51:22.078
Are you in your right mind?

51:22.788 --> 51:25.123
- We have to run!
- Hold it right there!

51:25.207 --> 51:26.917
- Hey!
- I'm not done with you!

51:27.000 --> 51:28.835
Why did you have to bring me along?

51:28.919 --> 51:30.295
I have no reason to run!

51:30.378 --> 51:32.631
I saved you from being beaten to a pulp.

51:32.714 --> 51:35.634
You're the only reason I got beaten
with a bunch of leeks!

51:35.717 --> 51:36.802
What's your plan now?

51:36.885 --> 51:38.804
Just think of it as playing tag.

51:38.887 --> 51:41.056
- Stop right there!
- We're dead if we get caught.

51:42.015 --> 51:42.849
Hey!

51:42.933 --> 51:44.351
I'm counting to ten!

51:44.935 --> 51:48.647
One, two, three, four,

51:48.730 --> 51:52.067
five, six, seven, eight,

51:52.150 --> 51:53.902
nine, ten!

51:55.821 --> 51:57.781
We're dead if we get caught, okay?

52:05.038 --> 52:07.332
Hey, get back here!

52:07.415 --> 52:09.668
Stop right there, Bae Seok-ryu!

52:14.089 --> 52:15.131
Hey!

52:15.757 --> 52:18.552
That little brat. Get back here!

52:23.390 --> 52:24.224
Hey.

52:25.976 --> 52:29.145
She wouldn't follow us here, right?

52:29.229 --> 52:32.440
We shook her off a long time ago.

52:32.524 --> 52:35.652
Then why didn't you tell me?
We could've stopped running.

52:35.735 --> 52:37.279
Why did we come all the way here?

52:38.738 --> 52:40.282
I'm totally wiped!

52:40.991 --> 52:42.158
Don't slap me away like that.

52:42.242 --> 52:44.369
You're the one who grabbed my hand first.

52:46.288 --> 52:47.247
Hey.

52:47.330 --> 52:48.540
Buy me something to drink.

52:48.623 --> 52:49.749
Are you nuts?

52:50.292 --> 52:51.418
The store is down there!

52:51.501 --> 52:54.421
I'm so thirsty right now
that I might puke.

52:54.504 --> 52:55.922
Swallow your spit.

52:56.006 --> 52:57.007
You heartless jerk.

53:00.886 --> 53:01.970
I'm exhausted.

53:02.929 --> 53:05.682
You should work out more
if you're exhausted from that.

53:06.600 --> 53:09.060
You try sitting in front of a computer
for ten years

53:09.603 --> 53:12.022
and see if your body comes out unscathed.

53:12.105 --> 53:14.691
That's still just an excuse.
You could've worked out more.

53:14.774 --> 53:16.443
It's so hot.

53:16.526 --> 53:18.153
Why isn't there any wind?

53:20.488 --> 53:21.740
Come here for a second.

53:21.823 --> 53:24.618
What now? What are you doing?

53:24.701 --> 53:25.869
Stand right here.

53:26.953 --> 53:30.832
Are you seriously going to use me
as your human shield again?

53:30.916 --> 53:32.334
You're my changing room this time.

53:32.417 --> 53:33.919
Hide me while I take these off.

53:35.378 --> 53:36.922
Why are you doing this to me?

53:44.638 --> 53:46.097
Jeez.

53:48.308 --> 53:52.062
How many layers did you wear?
Are you a nesting doll or something?

53:52.562 --> 53:53.563
What's that?

53:53.647 --> 53:56.149
You know, the Russian toy
that has dolls inside dolls.

53:58.318 --> 53:59.694
Are you saying I look like a doll?

54:00.445 --> 54:02.030
More like a dolt.

54:02.113 --> 54:03.281
I will end you.

54:03.365 --> 54:05.116
Just finish your shedding.

54:05.617 --> 54:07.827
I'm letting you off
for so many things today.

54:20.966 --> 54:22.050
Can I turn around?

54:24.803 --> 54:26.137
Hey, I'm turning around.

54:34.229 --> 54:36.022
Why didn't you answer me?

54:38.274 --> 54:39.734
I should've listened to you.

54:42.237 --> 54:44.489
Now Mom won't talk to me for a whole day.

54:45.365 --> 54:47.117
I'd say two days.

54:48.827 --> 54:50.036
That sucks.

54:51.121 --> 54:53.999
I should've looked more closely
at my mom's face then.

54:55.375 --> 54:56.584
I missed her.

54:58.753 --> 54:59.963
You should've been honest.

55:00.046 --> 55:02.382
Why did you tell her that you cheated?

55:04.509 --> 55:05.510
You don't believe

55:06.052 --> 55:07.137
that I cheated?

55:08.680 --> 55:09.681
Why not?

55:11.057 --> 55:14.519
Maybe I'm an irresistible femme fatale.

55:16.271 --> 55:17.480
- You?
- Hey.

55:18.064 --> 55:22.777
You shouldn't judge a book by its cover.

55:22.861 --> 55:23.862
The truth is…

55:25.613 --> 55:27.782
I'm hiding something huge.

55:29.117 --> 55:30.827
Just keep hiding it then.

55:31.661 --> 55:32.912
You're so annoying.

55:32.996 --> 55:34.497
Fine, I don't care.

55:34.581 --> 55:36.958
You won't guess in a million years anyway.

55:37.042 --> 55:40.295
It doesn't affect me at all.
I'm completely fine.

55:40.378 --> 55:42.172
You don't seem fine.

55:46.092 --> 55:49.304
You made two huge life decisions at once.

55:49.387 --> 55:52.057
Only a doll would be undamaged by that.

55:54.350 --> 55:56.269
So you really think I'm a doll, don't you?

55:59.564 --> 56:01.274
Maybe a satanic doll.

56:01.357 --> 56:02.442
Shut up.

56:11.951 --> 56:12.952
I just…

56:15.038 --> 56:17.290
felt like my life was getting overheated.

56:19.542 --> 56:21.169
You know how hard I've worked.

56:23.129 --> 56:24.672
I was studying in Korea,

56:25.340 --> 56:27.342
then I suddenly went to the US

56:27.425 --> 56:28.802
and had to adapt to that life.

56:29.427 --> 56:30.428
Then I got a job

56:31.012 --> 56:32.013
and got engaged too.

56:33.723 --> 56:35.850
Going at full throttle
all the time like that…

56:38.019 --> 56:39.687
overloaded my CPU.

56:41.314 --> 56:42.482
The screen went blank,

56:43.525 --> 56:45.110
and the keys stopped working.

56:46.736 --> 56:47.737
So I had no choice

56:49.364 --> 56:51.199
but to reboot myself.

56:56.037 --> 56:58.915
That was my excuse for quitting my job
and calling off my engagement.

57:03.753 --> 57:04.754
That was brave of you.

57:05.672 --> 57:06.631
It was.

57:07.423 --> 57:10.051
So I had to come back
before my courage expired

57:11.052 --> 57:13.930
and my resolve crumbled into nothing.

57:19.269 --> 57:22.522
Excuse me. Could you take a photo of us?

57:22.605 --> 57:24.482
- Sure.
- Thank you.

57:26.109 --> 57:26.985
Over there.

57:30.488 --> 57:31.865
- On three.
- Okay.

57:32.449 --> 57:33.783
One, two, three.

57:34.742 --> 57:35.827
Take a horizontal one too.

57:35.910 --> 57:36.911
Okay.

57:39.205 --> 57:40.832
One, two, three.

57:42.709 --> 57:43.543
- Here.
- Thanks.

57:43.626 --> 57:44.878
Thank you.

57:44.961 --> 57:46.254
Do you want a photo too?

57:46.337 --> 57:47.297
- No.
- No, thank you.

57:47.922 --> 57:49.174
It was as if on cue.

57:49.757 --> 57:51.426
You guys are totally in sync.

57:51.509 --> 57:54.179
You must have dated a long time
to get that way.

57:54.262 --> 57:55.263
- No, we're not…
- No.

57:56.931 --> 57:58.391
Then how do you know each other?

57:58.975 --> 58:00.185
He's the son of my mom's friend.

58:00.268 --> 58:01.478
She's the daughter of my mom's friend.

58:03.229 --> 58:04.856
- Goodbye, then.
- Thank you.

58:14.032 --> 58:15.283
It's Dong-jin.

58:15.366 --> 58:16.534
Hey, wait!

58:17.660 --> 58:18.870
Hello?

58:18.953 --> 58:22.207
Mom wants Seok-ryu to come home.
She says she won't hit her anymore.

58:23.249 --> 58:24.334
She's out of energy.

58:25.460 --> 58:27.629
Is that so? All right.

58:29.672 --> 58:30.507
What did he say?

58:31.591 --> 58:33.343
Your mother calmed down

58:33.426 --> 58:34.594
and wants you back home.

58:35.220 --> 58:36.721
- You're lying.
- I'm not.

58:36.804 --> 58:38.681
She's not going to be violent anymore

58:38.765 --> 58:40.934
and wants to resolve this peacefully.

58:41.017 --> 58:43.186
And I'm saying I don't believe her.

58:43.269 --> 58:45.563
You saw how she broke her promise
to hear me out.

58:45.647 --> 58:47.690
She's only going to smack me again.

58:47.774 --> 58:50.151
She wouldn't.
She has bad shoulders and wrists.

58:51.152 --> 58:54.155
She looked healthy enough earlier
when she was going at it.

58:54.239 --> 58:55.698
I can come with you if you want.

58:56.282 --> 58:57.992
Why are you suddenly being nice?

58:58.076 --> 59:01.246
It's just that Aunt Mi-suk
likes me better than you.

59:03.248 --> 59:05.917
It's so annoying that I can't deny that.

59:06.000 --> 59:07.502
Wait up!

59:09.712 --> 59:10.838
Jeez.

59:21.307 --> 59:22.976
Good work today.

59:23.059 --> 59:25.144
Can you give this to the patient

59:25.228 --> 59:26.938
who came in with me earlier?

59:27.021 --> 59:28.773
Thank you. See you tomorrow.

59:30.358 --> 59:31.359
Excuse me.

59:32.193 --> 59:33.194
Oh, hello.

59:33.945 --> 59:35.280
How is your hand?

59:35.363 --> 59:36.948
It's fine.

59:38.199 --> 59:39.117
I'm sorry.

59:39.200 --> 59:41.327
I shouldn't have interfered like that.

59:41.411 --> 59:42.829
It's okay.

59:42.912 --> 59:45.915
You looked a little foolish,
but I have a soft spot for kindness.

59:46.416 --> 59:47.250
Goodbye then.

59:49.294 --> 59:51.879
- Excuse me.
- What is it now?

59:51.963 --> 59:54.716
Is it okay for me to ask your name?

59:54.799 --> 59:57.927
Listen. I've been a paramedic
for six years.

59:58.011 --> 01:00:01.389
Of all the people who have asked
for my name and number to thank me,

01:00:01.472 --> 01:00:03.391
no one actually got in touch with me.

01:00:03.474 --> 01:00:04.851
I will, though.

01:00:04.934 --> 01:00:06.561
But I'm not telling you.

01:00:06.644 --> 01:00:08.229
- Goodbye!
- Wait!

01:00:12.775 --> 01:00:14.360
JAESEUNG UNIVERSITY MEDICAL CENTER

01:00:16.654 --> 01:00:17.655
Here you go.

01:00:18.323 --> 01:00:19.490
What's this?

01:00:19.574 --> 01:00:22.869
The paramedic who brought you in
told me to give you this.

01:00:27.624 --> 01:00:29.208
They're glucose candies.

01:00:29.292 --> 01:00:31.461
Take them if you get dizzy
from low blood sugar.

01:00:32.045 --> 01:00:34.005
Don't drink alcohol anymore, okay?

01:00:34.797 --> 01:00:38.676
Call 911 right away if you need help.

01:00:54.817 --> 01:00:56.944
THE CHUNGWOO DAILY

01:00:57.028 --> 01:00:58.154
As for me…

01:01:00.114 --> 01:01:01.658
I have a soft spot for touching stories.

01:01:15.129 --> 01:01:15.963
Wait a second.

01:01:16.839 --> 01:01:17.799
Give me a minute.

01:01:21.260 --> 01:01:23.388
I'm not prepared yet.

01:01:23.471 --> 01:01:24.305
You'll never be.

01:01:24.889 --> 01:01:25.932
Hey, wait!

01:01:27.892 --> 01:01:29.185
Who is it?

01:01:29.268 --> 01:01:31.729
It's me, Aunt Mi-suk. I brought Seok-ryu.

01:01:32.313 --> 01:01:33.981
Okay. Come in.

01:01:37.110 --> 01:01:38.111
See?

01:01:41.906 --> 01:01:43.449
You go in first.

01:02:01.968 --> 01:02:03.469
I think she's crying.

01:02:06.180 --> 01:02:07.181
Mom.

01:02:09.517 --> 01:02:10.476
Are you crying?

01:02:13.146 --> 01:02:14.480
I'm sorry, Mom.

01:02:15.523 --> 01:02:16.691
Don't cry.

01:02:25.825 --> 01:02:26.659
Come here.

01:02:27.368 --> 01:02:28.828
Let's see this out to the end.

01:02:29.954 --> 01:02:30.955
Run!

01:02:31.998 --> 01:02:32.999
What are you doing?

01:02:33.499 --> 01:02:35.418
I brought her to you,

01:02:35.501 --> 01:02:37.044
so do whatever you want with her.

01:02:39.922 --> 01:02:42.425
Hey! That little… Open up!

01:02:42.508 --> 01:02:43.676
Open up!

01:02:46.596 --> 01:02:48.681
Come on, open the door.

01:02:48.765 --> 01:02:52.185
I should've known you'd betray me!
You're dead meat tomorrow!

01:02:52.268 --> 01:02:53.436
Tomorrow?

01:02:53.519 --> 01:02:55.605
Do you think you'll be alive tomorrow?

01:02:55.688 --> 01:02:56.522
Mom.

01:02:57.273 --> 01:02:59.108
Just hear me out.

01:02:59.192 --> 01:03:01.819
- Come inside.
- Getting mad is bad for your health.

01:03:02.403 --> 01:03:04.989
Okay, fine! Mom!

01:03:05.072 --> 01:03:06.824
- Come here.
- Mom!

01:03:06.908 --> 01:03:09.619
Just tell it to me straight!
What happened?

01:03:09.702 --> 01:03:10.870
Just tell me!

01:03:18.711 --> 01:03:21.214
Is it true that you can't speak Korean?

01:03:21.297 --> 01:03:23.591
It's because he was born abroad.

01:03:23.674 --> 01:03:25.218
Then say something in a foreign language.

01:03:25.301 --> 01:03:26.677
Come on!

01:03:26.761 --> 01:03:28.471
Looks like he can't do anything.

01:03:29.305 --> 01:03:30.807
Are you dumb?

01:03:31.390 --> 01:03:32.391
Hey!

01:03:32.892 --> 01:03:33.851
It's Bae Seok-ryu.

01:03:34.435 --> 01:03:37.104
She'll kill you
if you make fun of this idiot.

01:03:37.188 --> 01:03:39.065
What did you just say?

01:03:39.649 --> 01:03:40.817
Say it again.

01:03:41.859 --> 01:03:45.029
I'll kill you if you bother my baby again!

01:03:49.909 --> 01:03:52.954
Now that she's back,
it's going to get chaotic again.

01:03:53.037 --> 01:03:56.958
You already hit me there, Mom!
Hit me somewhere else!

01:03:57.708 --> 01:03:59.669
Does it hurt? Then you know how I feel!

01:03:59.752 --> 01:04:01.671
You're about to reach your 60th birthday.

01:04:01.754 --> 01:04:03.464
Shouldn't that make you more lenient?

01:04:11.138 --> 01:04:13.099
Just hear me out, please!

01:04:13.182 --> 01:04:15.810
It hurts!

01:04:15.893 --> 01:04:17.645
COMEBACK

01:04:17.728 --> 01:04:23.568
COME BACK HOME

01:04:55.850 --> 01:05:00.229
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:05:00.313 --> 01:05:03.316
I basically raised Seung-hyo.

01:05:03.399 --> 01:05:05.860
Don't trust her.
Every word she says is a lie.

01:05:05.943 --> 01:05:07.361
This girl was

01:05:07.445 --> 01:05:10.531
the first lunatic I met in my life.

01:05:10.615 --> 01:05:13.951
I can't believe that picky little kid
grew up to be such a successful man.

01:05:14.702 --> 01:05:15.703
I'm proud of you.

01:05:15.786 --> 01:05:17.246
Seok-ryu.

01:05:17.330 --> 01:05:18.164
What are you doing here?

01:05:18.664 --> 01:05:20.124
You don't want me here, do you?

01:05:20.207 --> 01:05:22.001
You never wanted me to come back.

01:05:22.084 --> 01:05:23.502
That's why you got rid of my room.

01:05:24.420 --> 01:05:25.838
I turned back time.

01:05:26.380 --> 01:05:28.007
I recreated your embarrassing past.

01:05:30.176 --> 01:05:35.181
Subtitle translation by: Ji-yeun Kim
